extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_RUMOURED_TERROR_GROUP: A Rumoured Terror Group
    STR_RUMOURED_TERROR_GROUP_UFOPEDIA: 'For a year the agencies have traded stories about a new terrorist outfit: well armed, well paid, and gone by the time anyone arrives. No name, no photograph, no
      defectors.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hawk says money and guns always leave a trail. I say anyone this careful has made one mistake somewhere. Either way we start with a border cartel carrying hardware it cannot
      afford.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_CARTEL_LEDGER: Cartel Ledger
    STR_CARTEL_LEDGER_UFOPEDIA: 'The boss kept honest books, which is more than his customers did. Drugs, bribes, the usual. And one supplier with no name: cash in advance, paid through a bank on the border,
      and the guns delivered by air.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Somebody is arming a border cartel and doesn''t want to be known. That makes me want to know.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE: Crate Serial Plate
    STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE_UFOPEDIA: Roadblock read me the plate off a crate in the barn. The serial belongs to no army and no maker on any register we can reach. It carries a lot number, C-0417, that nobody
      admits to.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Someone stamps their own lot numbers. That's a factory, somewhere.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_COBRA_STENCIL: Cobra Stencil
    STR_COBRA_STENCIL_UFOPEDIA: 'Painted inside a crate lid, where the buyer was never meant to look: a coiled snake, hood spread. Not a cartel mark. Not anybody''s mark, as far as any file in The Pit knows.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Whoever
      packs these guns signs their work. That''s pride, or it''s a message.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_WHO_IS_COBRA: Who Is Cobra?
    STR_WHO_IS_COBRA_UFOPEDIA: 'The snake on those crates has a name: Cobra. No country, no cause I can find, and more money than any terrorist group has a right to.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}From today, anything
      we take from them goes to the lab, and anyone we take from them comes to me.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS_INTERROGATION: Cartel Boss Interrogation
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'The boss is a businessman and he bargained like one. He gave us his next flight: the plane, the strip and the night. He also let slip that his supplier''s ''new
      owners'' want their plant back on a fixed date. He doesn''t know where the plant is. He does know the date.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He sold me both for a better cell. Cheap at the price.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He
      threw in one more thing for free, to show he could: his people are holding an Army driver at their chop shop outside the border town. They took his vehicle and kept him to make it run. Somebody should
      go and get him.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_FACTORY_SCHEDULE: Factory Production Schedule
    STR_FACTORY_SCHEDULE_UFOPEDIA: 'From the plant manager''s safe: a production schedule on letterhead with the snake on it. The lines restart, a guard detail arrives and the first shipment leaves, all
      on one date.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hawk has circled it. So have I.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_FACTORY_REACTIVATION_DATE: Factory Reactivation Date
    STR_FACTORY_REACTIVATION_DATE_UFOPEDIA: We know when Cobra takes the West Texas plant back. Hit it before then and the lines never start. Hit it on the day and it will be guarded. Leave it, and its
      rifles will be in Cobra hands within months.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hawk's call. My advice is before.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_TRACE_THE_BROADCAST: Trace the Broadcast
    STR_TRACE_THE_BROADCAST_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra Commander has introduced himself to the world: a hooded man, a snake banner and ninety seconds of threats. Breaker took the signal apart. Three relays, and whoever
      set up the first one got lazy.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}It leads to one building and one Cobra cell. A cell, not a headquarters. But cells are full of people, and people talk.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_EXTENSIVE_ENTERPRISES: Extensive Enterprises
    STR_EXTENSIVE_ENTERPRISES_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra''s money runs through one company: Extensive Enterprises. Warehouses, shipping lines, offices in three countries, and every one of them clean on paper. The
      owners of record are twin brothers, Tomax and Xamot Paoli. Their signatures on the board minutes match to the pen stroke.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Their offices and warehouses can now be raided.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}-
      Scarlett'
    STR_CARTEL_FLIGHT_ROUTE: Cartel Flight Route
    STR_CARTEL_FLIGHT_ROUTE_UFOPEDIA: 'The cartel''s next flight is on the board: the plane, the strip and the night. Shoot it down and we get a wreck. Follow it home and we get their stash house.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hawk
      wants it followed. So do I.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_CARTEL_LOGBOOK: Cartel Pilot's Logbook
    STR_CARTEL_LOGBOOK_UFOPEDIA: 'We shot it down, so the pilot can''t show us the way home. His logbook can. Every run ends at the same strip outside the same town: the cartel''s stash house.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}It
      took longer than following him would have.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_INFORMANT_TIP: Informant's Tip
    STR_INFORMANT_TIP_UFOPEDIA: 'My courier at the stash house came through. The cartel lost a fortune at the ranch and means to make it back fast: an armored car, a payroll run, and a date.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We''ll
      be there first.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_ROBBERY_LEADER: Robbery Leader
    STR_ROBBERY_LEADER_INTERROGATION: Robbery Leader Interrogation
    STR_ROBBERY_LEADER_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: The crew boss knows nothing about guns and everything about money. The cartel washes its cash through one bank on the border, and every month that bank pays
      a company in West Texas that hasn't made anything in two years.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_GETAWAY_PAPERS: Getaway Papers
    STR_GETAWAY_PAPERS_UFOPEDIA: 'Paperwork from the getaway van: a deposit book from a bank on the border and a list of account numbers the crew was told to pay into. Somebody forgot to tell them not to
      write it down.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_BORDER_BANK_TRACE: 'Follow the Money: the Border Bank'
    STR_BORDER_BANK_TRACE_UFOPEDIA: 'My analysts walked the cartel''s money through the border bank, and every trail ends at one account: a machine works on a rail spur in West Texas. Bankrupt for two years,
      still being paid. Lot C-0417 came out of there.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Whoever armed the cartel built those guns in that factory. Hawk is planning the visit.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_LEAD_CARTEL_SUPPLIER: Who supplies the cartel?
    STR_FOLLOW_THE_MONEY: Follow the Money
    STR_FOLLOW_THE_MONEY_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra washes its cash before it spends it: through the Twins'' companies, a few friendly banks, and anywhere that takes a lot of money and asks no questions. Washed money
      leaves cold trails.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The bank wrappers and Extensive Enterprises'' books give us the method. My analysts can now trace laundered cash back to where it was washed, and with enough paper
      Washington can freeze the accounts.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_MAJOR_BLUDD: Major Bludd
    STR_MAJOR_BLUDD_UFOPEDIA: Sebastian Bludd. Mercenary, Australian, poet by his own account, and Cobra's now. He left a card behind with the names of the Joes who got in his way and a promise, in verse,
      to see each of them again.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The verse is bad. The promise I'm taking seriously.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_SHIPPING_MANIFEST: Shipping Manifest
    STR_SHIPPING_MANIFEST_UFOPEDIA: A manifest for cargo that doesn't exist, from a company that doesn't trade, to a warehouse that keeps turning up in other papers.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}One piece of paper
      is a curiosity. I'm collecting them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_PILOT_LOGBOOK: Pilot's Logbook
    STR_PILOT_LOGBOOK_UFOPEDIA: 'A Cobra pilot''s logbook: times, fuel and landing strips in a private shorthand. Private to him, anyway. Once you have the key it reads like a bus timetable.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}-
      Scarlett'
    STR_DEPOT_ROUTE_ANALYSIS: Depot Route Analysis
    STR_DEPOT_ROUTE_ANALYSIS_UFOPEDIA: 'I put the manifests, the logbook, the fuel receipts and the bills of lading on one map. The same handful of places keeps coming up. Without an officer to confirm
      it this took longer, but I''d stake my stripes on it: depots.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_COBRA_DEPOTS: Cobra Depots
    STR_COBRA_DEPOTS_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra''s flights and trucks don''t run cell to cell. They run to depots: warehouses where guns, money and men are gathered and sent on.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We can find them
      now. A depot found is a depot raided.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_DEPOT_RECORDS: Depot Records
    STR_DEPOT_RECORDS_UFOPEDIA: Records from the depot we hit. Most of the stock went out to the cells, as expected. A fixed share of everything went somewhere else, and no address is given.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Nobody
      skims that neatly unless they're told to.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett
    STR_TERROR_DROME_RUMOURS: Rumours of a Terror Drome
    STR_TERROR_DROME_RUMOURS_UFOPEDIA: 'Every depot sends its share to the same place, and none of our sources has seen it. Prisoners call it the Drome: a fortress with its own air wing, they say, and nearly
      finished.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}From now on every captured document gets read for one thing: how close.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_TERROR_DROME_PLANS: Terror Drome Defense Plans
    STR_TERROR_DROME_PLANS_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra''s first Terror Drome, on paper: gun positions, the Firebat launch bay, the garrison rota, and where it is. Hawk is drawing up the assault.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}I''ve
      told him what the plans can''t. They will know these are missing.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_MARS_MARKINGS: M.A.R.S. Markings
    STR_MARS_MARKINGS_UFOPEDIA: 'Roadblock found it on a rifle from the Drome, under Cobra''s paint: a maker''s mark. M.A.R.S., Military Armaments Research Syndicate.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Cobra doesn''t build
      its own guns. Somebody sells them, and a seller that size never has just one customer. I want to know who signs his invoices.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett'
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS: Cartel Boss
    STR_BROADCAST_RECORDING: Broadcast Recording
    STR_BLUDD_CALLING_CARD: Bludd's Calling Card
    STR_MARS_MARKED_WEAPON: M.A.R.S.-Marked Weapon
